@startuml
title US-001 - Register organization and admin - SD level 3 - Frontend
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 75
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF2F8
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #FEF9E7
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
autonumber

actor "Prospective Admin" as Admin
participant "RegisterPage" as View
participant "RegisterForm" as Component
participant "ConfirmEmailPage" as Confirm
participant "authService" as Service
participant "HttpClient" as Http
participant "Nexo API" as API

note over View, API
  RegisterForm is a two-step wizard (organization name, then admin details and
  password); only the final step submits. A 202 means "check your email" for
  a new and an already registered email alike.
end note

Admin -> View: Submit organization, admin details, and password
activate View
View -> Component: handleSubmit(organizationName, adminFirstName, adminLastName, adminEmail, password)
activate Component
Component -> Service: register(dto)
activate Service
Service -> Http: POST /organizations (RegisterOrganizationDto)
activate Http
Http -> API: HTTP request
activate API
alt Request accepted
    API --> Http: 202 Accepted
else Request rejected
    API --> Http: 400/409/429/500
end
deactivate API
Http --> Service: Response or rejected request
deactivate Http
Service --> Component: void, or thrown error
deactivate Service
alt Successful response
    Component --> View: Navigate to /login?registered=1 ("check your email")
else Failed response
    Component --> View: Error state (validation / operation failure)
end
deactivate Component
View --> Admin: Render the resulting state
deactivate View

Admin -> Confirm: Open /confirm-email?email&token (from the email)
activate Confirm
Confirm -> Service: confirmEmail(email, token), sent once on open
activate Service
Service -> Http: POST /accounts/activation/confirm-email
activate Http
Http -> API: HTTP request
activate API
alt Confirmed
    API --> Http: 200 OK
else Link not valid
    API --> Http: 403 Forbidden
end
deactivate API
Http --> Service: Response or rejected request
deactivate Http
Service --> Confirm: void, or thrown error
deactivate Service
alt Confirmed
    Confirm --> Admin: Navigate to /login?confirmed=1
else Not valid
    Confirm --> Admin: Explain the link is not valid; link back to sign-in
end
deactivate Confirm
@enduml
